# A static Go build, which is how Go programs are built; there is no shared
# library here to link against. Upstream's own Linux release became a static
# build in 3.28.1 -- 3.26.0 was dynamically linked, which is what the
# hardening-no-pie and undeclared-elf-prerequisites overrides here used to be
# for. See debian/rules and README.md.
vale: statically-linked-binary [usr/bin/vale]

# Not an upload to Debian: this package lives in a private Forgejo registry
# and tracks upstream releases, so no bug is ever closed by its first entry.
vale: initial-upload-closes-no-bugs
